<title>USA: GENERAL MOTORS UNIT FILES $4.2 BLN SHELF.</title>
<headline>GENERAL MOTORS UNIT FILES $4.2 BLN SHELF.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>General Motors Acceptance Corp, a financing unit of General Motors Corp, filed Friday with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission to register a shelf offering of up to $4.2 billion in debt securities and warrants to purchase debt securities.</p>
<p>Together with previously registered securities, the shelf offering totals $5 billion.</p>
<p>Proceeds from the sale will be used by the financing arm for general corporate needs, including purchasing receivables and repaying outstanding debt.</p>
<p>No underwriters were named in the shelf offering.</p>
</text>
